    "body": "## Summary\n\ndivine-mobile #4283 and divine-web #364 split the single \"Child Safety Violation\" report reason into three distinct categories with distinct NIP-32 labels. The relay-manager `CATEGORY_LABELS` map in `src/lib/constants.ts` needs entries for the two new labels so they render as human-readable names instead of raw strings in the moderator UI.\n\nReports work correctly without this — the raw label strings are displayed and reports are fully functional. This is a cosmetic improvement for moderators.\n\n## What's needed\n\nAdd to `CATEGORY_LABELS`:\n- `'NS-childSafety'`: `'Child Safety'`\n- `'childSafety'`: `'Child Safety'`\n- `'child-safety'`: `'Child Safety'`\n- `'NS-child-safety'`: `'Child Safety'`\n- `'NS-underageUser'`: `'Under 16'`\n- `'underageUser'`: `'Under 16'`\n- `'underage-user'`: `'Under 16'`\n- `'NS-underage-user'`: `'Under 16'`\n\nBoth camelCase and kebab-case aliases are needed (mobile emits camelCase, web emits kebab-case). Follows the existing pattern for `NS-sexualContent` / `NS-sexual-content`.\n\nAlso consider whether `NS-childSafety` / `NS-child-safety` should be added to `HIGH_PRIORITY_CATEGORIES` (media auto-hidden for moderator safety).\n\n`NS-csam` is already mapped and in the high-priority list — no changes needed there.\n\n## Context\n\n- divine-mobile #4283\n- divine-web #364\n- divine-mobile #3489\n- support-trust-safety #107",
